      "content": "<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out the answer. The user wants the gender split from the 2011 Bulgarian census about tertiary education. The initial search for the Wikipedia entry didn't work because it returned Croatia's data. Then, using Google search, I found a link to the NSI's census report. The extracted text from that link mentions \"791.8 thousand women (22.3%) and...\" which suggests that 791.8 thousand women had completed tertiary education. But I need the number for men too.\n\nWait, the snippet from the NSI PDF says \"791.8 thousand women (22.3%) and 615.3 thousand men (17.7%)\". So the numbers are 791.8k for women and 615.3k for men. Subtracting the smaller (615.3k) from the larger (791.8k) gives 176.5 thousand. The answer should be in thousands of women, so the difference is 176.5. \n\nBut I need to confirm that the NSI PDF has these exact numbers. The extracted text from the URL seems to have the figures, but I should check if the percentages are for the same total population. If the total population is 7,300,000 (as per the 2011 census), then 22.3% of women would be 791.8k and 17.7% of men would be 615.3k. The difference is 791.8 - 615.3 = 176.5 thousand women. \n\nSince the NSI's document is the official source, the numbers are likely accurate. Therefore, the final answer should be 176.5.\n</think>\n\n<reflection>\nThe extracted text from the NSI's 2011 census PDF provides the absolute numbers: 791.8 thousand women (22.3%) and 615.3 thousand men (17.7%) with tertiary education. The difference is 791.8 - 615.3 = 176.5 thousand women. The task is complete as the required data is now available.\n</reflection>\n\n<answer>\n176.5\n</answer>",
